Section cap helper, also executed:
  _REPORT_BUDGET = 120_000
  def _cap_sections(md, budget=_REPORT_BUDGET):
      if len(md) <= budget: return md, []
      kept, dropped, used = [], [], 0
      for ch in re.split(r'(?m)^(?=## )', md):
          name = ch.splitlines()[0][3:].strip() if ch.startswith('## ') else '(preamble)'
          if used + len(ch) <= budget or not kept:
              kept.append(ch); used += len(ch)
          else:
              dropped.append(name)
      return ''.join(kept), dropped
It cuts only on a `## ` boundary, so no table is ever left half-rendered.
